# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
config RUST_SOFTIRQ
	bool "Rust softirq dispatch, tasklets and interrupt context"
	depends on RUST && X86_64
	depends on !RANDSTRUCT && !CFI && !GCC_PLUGIN_LATENT_ENTROPY
	default y
	help
	  Select Rust as the sole algorithm/data owner of kernel/softirq.o,
	  including RT and non-RT BH state, dispatch, IRQ context, tasklets,
	  CPU hotplug, softirq/timer daemons and weak IRQ setup defaults.
	  Configured types are generated from the original kernel headers.
	  A native companion emits compiler trace/export/initcall metadata,
	  architecture/atomic operations and explicitly recorded remaining
	  header/subsystem migration dependencies.

	  This selector describes the intended supported x86_64 source scope;
	  a source-only proposal is not evidence of successful compilation or
	  runtime equivalence. The recorded validation gates must pass before
	  accepting any production configuration, including tracing and RT.
	  Original C is retained for deliberate reference/test configurations.
	  Rust production validation must reject an unset selector, C fallback
	  or a duplicate C owner. Other architectures, CFI, randstruct and GCC
	  latent-entropy instrumentation require further work.
